        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): drain root work continuations before stop process exit",
        "body": "#### What Problem This Solves\n\nClose #105697\n\nWhen a gateway process receives a direct stop signal (SIGTERM/SIGINT without a restart intent), any `session_end` plugin hooks already started by session reset/delete/compaction may be truncated before they complete. Affected plugins may lose database writes, memory summaries, or external resource cleanups.\n\n#### Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a bounded drain of the existing gateway root-work set to the direct-stop path. The drain uses a referenced `setTimeout` poll (not `.unref()`) so the timer keeps the event loop alive. Bounded at 2 seconds; the caller always invokes `exitProcess(0)` after return. Per ClawSweeper clarification: the force-exit watchdog is cleared at `run-loop.ts:705` before `handleStopAfterServerClose` is entered at line 710; the drain is self-bounded by its own referenced timer.\n\n#### User Impact\n\nNo visible impact. Pending `session_end` hooks get up to 2 seconds to complete before exit. Stuck hooks cannot block shutdown.\n\n#### Evidence\n\n**1. Real Gateway startup + shutdown log (PR branch, 10 production plugins, Node v22.23.1)**\n\n```\n[gateway] loading configuration…\n[gateway] resolving authentication…\n[gateway] starting...\n[secrets] [***S_REF_IGNORED_INACTIVE_SURFACE] channels.discord.***: no enabled account inherits this top-level Discord ***.\n[gateway] session: imported legacy session metadata/transcripts into SQLite:\n- targets=1 legacyEntries=8 sqliteEntries=8\n- importedEntries=8 importedTranscriptEvents=0\n[gateway] session: session SQLite migration warnings:\n- [entry_invalid] agent:main:cron:4fa39e4c-188d-411d-a223-a81128de1695: Session entry is missing a valid sessionId.\n[gateway] starting HTTP server...\n[gateway] ⚠️  Gateway is binding to a non-loopback address. Ensure authentication is configured before exposing to public networks.\n[health-monitor] started (interval: 300s, startup-grace: 60s, channel-connect-grace: 120s)\n[gateway] agent model: vendor/model-name (thinking=off, fast=off)\n[gateway] http server listening (10 plugins: acpx, anthropic, browser, canvas, device-pair,\n           file-transfer, memory-core, ollama, phone-control, talk-voice; 8.7s)\n[gateway] log file: /tmp/openclaw/openclaw-YYYY-MM-DD.log\n[gateway] security warning: dangerous config flags enabled: gateway.controlUi.allowInsecureAuth=true,\n           gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyDisableDeviceAuth=true. Run `openclaw security audit`.\n[gateway] starting channels and sidecars...\n[hooks] loaded 4 internal hook handlers\n[plugins] embedded acpx runtime backend registered lazily\n[gateway] startup outcomes: internal-hooks=loaded; internal-startup-hook=scheduled;\n           gateway-start-hooks=scheduled; memory-qmd=skipped (not-configured);\n           gmail-watcher=skipped (hooks-disabled); gmail-model=skipped (not-configured)\n[gateway] ready\n[heartbeat] started\n[gateway] agent runtime plugins pre-warmed in 187ms\n\n                                 … gateway running, channels connected …\n\n[gateway] received SIGTERM; shutting down\n[gmail-watcher] gmail watcher stopped\n[shutdown] completed cleanly in 261ms\n```\n\nGateway under this PR starts cleanly with 10 production plugins (including acpx, browser, canvas, device-pair, file-transfer, memory-core, ollama, phone-control, talk-voice), reaches ready state, and shuts down in 261ms with zero errors.\n\n**2. Drain mechanism proof (12/12 passed)**\n\nEach case: real child process, real `gateway-work-admission` module, real OS SIGTERM, real `waitForGatewayRootWorkDrain()`. Continuations created via the same `root.run()` → `runWithGatewayIndependentRootWorkContinuation()` → `root.release()` pattern as `session-reset-service.ts`.\n\n```\n=== Gateway Drain — Real Process Proof ===\n\n[Case 1] No hooks:         exit=0 20ms\n[Case 2] 350ms hook+SIGTERM: exit=0 315ms  sentinel=done 1783951839244\n[Case 3] Stuck hook:       exit=0 1020ms\n[Case 4] 2 concurrent:     exit=0 364ms\n\n=== 12/12 passed ===\n```\n\n- Case 2: continuation mid-flight when SIGTERM arrives → drain blocks until hook writes file → file confirmed on disk. Without the drain fix, Node exits before the 350ms write.\n- Case 3: never-releasing hook → drain returns false after 1s timeout → exits cleanly\n- Case 4: two concurrent hooks → drain waits for slowest → both files confirmed\n\n**3. Unit tests (62 passed)**\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/process/gateway-work-admission.test.ts src/cli/gateway-cli/run-loop.test.ts\n✓ |unit| src/process/gateway-work-admission.test.ts (17 tests)\n✓ |cli|  src/cli/gateway-cli/run-loop.test.ts (45 tests)\nTest Files 2 passed (2) | Tests 62 passed (62)\n```\n\n**4. Change scope:** 4 files, +116 lines. No config, CLI, SDK, docs, or changelog surface. No new dependencies.",
